# Security headers for Tanawin Finance (Cloudflare Pages).
#
# Cloudflare consumes this file as configuration rather than serving it, so
# /_headers itself should return 404 on the live site. Lives in public/ because
# Next copies that directory to the root of the deploy output, which is where
# Cloudflare looks for it.
#
# CSP IS ENFORCING (flipped 2026-09-01, after the report-only stage).
#
# How it was cleared before enforcing: the demo dataset was built in PRODUCTION
# mode and served locally with this exact policy applied as an ENFORCING meta
# tag — stricter than a report-only header, so a violation breaks the screen
# rather than whispering to a console nobody is watching. Every screen was then
# walked in all three roles (admin, staff, guest): dashboard, review, new, pcf,
# notes, users/categories/vendors manage, entries, an entry with a receipt
# photo, gallery, a gallery receipt, categories, the Excel export and the
# receipts ZIP. Zero securitypolicyviolation events, no broken images, both
# downloads produced their file. The dev server is NOT usable for this — it
# uses eval() for hot-reload and reports script-src violations that could never
# happen on the deployed bundle.
#
# If a future change adds a CDN, a font host, an image host or realtime (wss),
# it MUST be added here or it will be blocked in production and nowhere else.
#
# How each directive was chosen (verified against the live bundle, not assumed):
#   script-src 'unsafe-inline' — the App Router ships its hydration payload as
#     8 inline <script> blocks with no nonce. Next cannot nonce these without
#     middleware, so this is unavoidable short of that change. Be honest about
#     what it costs: this CSP does NOT stop an injected inline script. What it
#     does buy is blocking EXTERNAL script loads, constraining where the page
#     may send data (connect-src), and refusing to be framed.
#   'unsafe-eval' deliberately absent — the production chunks contain no eval().
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline' — the dashboard/analytics bars set widths and
#     heights via inline style props; without this the charts render flat.
#   img-src data: — receipt photos are base64 data URLs stored in the database.
#     Remove this and every receipt image in the app disappears.
#   connect-src — 'self' covers /version.json (the update check); the Supabase
#     origin is the only other host the app talks to. No wss: realtime is not
#     used anywhere. Add it here if that ever changes.
#   frame-ancestors 'none' — same intent as X-Frame-Options, for browsers that
#     honour CSP instead.
#
# Permissions-Policy: camera=() is safe here, CONFIRMED on a real phone
# 2026-09-01 — receipt capture still opens the camera. It uses
# <input type="file" capture="environment">, which goes through the OS file
# picker and is not governed by the camera permission (that gates
# getUserMedia, which this app never calls).

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://gzijmkzwnfebgaqxcrbh.supabase.co; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
